      "id": "D6",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL: dual_over_all_queries quantifies over EVERY query, and quadratic_inf_Icc turns the CONTINUOUS x-range into a three-point check, so the alternative family is now a finite check in x.  The family is still (d,x) and is declared"
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "status": "OPEN",
      "verdict": "OPEN: kept as a side model; no transfer to the Functional complexity is claimed"
    },
    {
      "id": "Q3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL: the Gaussian derivatives, the level cancellation, the NON-VANISHING of Delta_r, the Cauchy-Schwarz lower bound, the integrable envelope AND the uniform Taylor remainder (bound_of_vanishing_derivs) are now all proved, together with the chi2 assembly H^2 <= (J/2)h^{2r}.  The ONE remaining step is bookkeeping: iteratedDeriv of a finite SUM, for which Mathlib has no lemma"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL: the peeling budget telescopes to delta, the union bound is proved in a measure space, and a geometric tail bounds the expected stopping time.  The per-(arm,count) CONCENTRATION inequality is still an input, and the tracking step is still open"
    },
    {
      "id": "G2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL: the clean-build script now ARCHIVES every local .olean, log and receipt in the closure to legacy/ (never deletes) and rebuilds; 29/29 accepted with all hashes matching.  mathlib stays pinned by rev"
    },
